  "limitations": {
    "cache_admission": "NewStrictClientSet requires rpc.AsyncCache capability; production standalone AsyncSourceRPCRequestCache implements prepared admission. Transaction-bound adapters reject async construction; source sync cache commits independently of business rollback. NewClientSet synchronous-only fallback retains weaker invocation-prefix timing. Native Store mutex serializes an executing write/read; source-vs-native concurrent cache-read visibility is not established. No real delayed source DB insertion/concurrent-read transcript is claimed; the M38 synthetic held-completion evidence is separate. PGlite cross-Store Backend.Begin waits shared backend mutex non-contextually, in addition to in-flight IO limits. No source commit-order or full concurrency parity claim.",
    "action_scope": "Typed revert data/status and zero-data causes, not full Viem wrapper/custom-error decode/message parity. Ten total empty-data attempts with125ms exponential/source message predicate; other not-found actions unsupported. AsyncRequester BeginCall enables chunk admission/all-settled; sync-only custom requester prefix is weaker. Existing ABI.Parse anonymous tuple encoding limitation remains. Source batched insert grouping versus native per-child calls not claimed equivalent.",
    "prefetch_profile_lru": "Not established by this bounded action proof; separate profile/prefetch evidence is required. Eight bounded public action originals only.",
    "static_gaps": "The three previous indexing TS-only obligations remain unmapped; no unrelated Go compiler tests substitute.",
    "rpc_boundary": "Actual source RPC request/response tapes replay the transport boundary; no native EVM implementation claimed."
  },
